{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25616842",
      "title": "Exploring Server-side Rendering (SSR) with \"getServerSideProps\"",
      "sourceHash": "c829e95f10b559926c96d5f7436a211856364766dd05cb5625d1565b4ef5607e",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.48,
          "end": 5.93,
          "en": "So getStaticProps is a very useful function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.93,
          "end": 8.792,
          "en": "which you can export in your page components to ensure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.792,
          "end": 12.178,
          "en": "that your pre-rendered pages contain data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.178,
          "end": 15.04,
          "en": "you might need to wait for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.04,
          "end": 17.32,
          "en": "Now with revalidate, you can ensure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.32,
          "end": 21.672,
          "en": "that this page is also updated regularly after deployment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.672,
          "end": 25.301,
          "en": "But sometimes even a regular update is not enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.301,
          "end": 29.061,
          "en": "Sometimes you really want to regenerate this page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.061,
          "end": 32.203,
          "en": "for every incoming request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.203,
          "end": 35.962,
          "en": "So you want to pre-generate the page dynamically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.962,
          "end": 40.058,
          "en": "on the fly after deployment on the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 40.058,
          "end": 41.813,
          "en": "Not during the build process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.813,
          "end": 44.03,
          "en": "and not every couple of seconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.03,
          "end": 46.05,
          "en": "but for every request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.05,
          "end": 47.54,
          "en": "And if that's your goal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.54,
          "end": 50.712,
          "en": "then there is an alternative to getStaticProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.712,
          "end": 53.411,
          "en": "Now, I will comment out getStaticProps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.411,
          "end": 55.683,
          "en": "because it is the better choice here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.683,
          "end": 57.461,
          "en": "and I wanna use it later again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.461,
          "end": 60.97,
          "en": "But I want to show you this alternative as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.97,
          "end": 63.82,
          "en": "And that would be another function which you can export.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.82,
          "end": 67.003,
          "en": "A function that can also be async if you want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.003,
          "end": 71.263,
          "en": "And that's the getServerSideProps function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.11,
          "end": 75.191,
          "en": "Just like getStaticProps, that is a reserved name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.191,
          "end": 77.58,
          "en": "which NextJS will be looking for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.58,
          "end": 80.42,
          "en": "And the difference to getStaticProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.42,
          "end": 83.53,
          "en": "is that this function will now not run",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.53,
          "end": 85.231,
          "en": "during the build process,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.231,
          "end": 89.944,
          "en": "but instead always on the server after deployment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.944,
          "end": 92.705,
          "en": "Now you will still return an object here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.705,
          "end": 95.311,
          "en": "an object with a props property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.311,
          "end": 98.42,
          "en": "because after all, this function still is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 98.42,
          "end": 101.648,
          "en": "about getting the props for this page component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.648,
          "end": 105.67,
          "en": "And you can still then fetch data from an API here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 105.67,
          "end": 108.458,
          "en": "or from the file system, whatever you want to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.458,
          "end": 112.61,
          "en": "Any code you write in here will always run on the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.61,
          "end": 113.999,
          "en": "never in the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.999,
          "end": 116.42099999999999,
          "en": "So you can run the server side code in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.42099999999999,
          "end": 119.63900000000001,
          "en": "you can also perform operations that use credentials",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.63900000000001,
          "end": 122.17,
          "en": "that should not be exposed to your users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 122.17,
          "end": 125.53,
          "en": "because this code only runs on the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.53,
          "end": 129.68,
          "en": "And then ultimately, you return your props object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 129.68,
          "end": 132.02100000000002,
          "en": "So here an object with a meetups key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 132.02100000000002,
          "end": 135.221,
          "en": "which holds my dummy meetups, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 135.221,
          "end": 138.01,
          "en": "Now you can't set revalidate here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.01,
          "end": 140.87,
          "en": "because it doesn't make any sense here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 140.87,
          "end": 143.36,
          "en": "This getServerSideProps function runs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 143.36,
          "end": 145.338,
          "en": "for every incoming requests anyways,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 145.338,
          "end": 149.349,
          "en": "so there is no need to revalidate every x seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.349,
          "end": 151.4,
          "en": "Now what you can do in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 151.4,
          "end": 154.62,
          "en": "is you can work with a parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 154.62,
          "end": 157.488,
          "en": "which you'll receive. The context parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 157.488,
          "end": 160.518,
          "en": "You actually also get this and getStaticProps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 160.518,
          "end": 163.678,
          "en": "but I will come back to it there, later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 163.678,
          "end": 167.23,
          "en": "You do get it here and getServerSideProps as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 167.23,
          "end": 170.4,
          "en": "And there in this context argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 170.4,
          "end": 172.036,
          "en": "in this context parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 172.036,
          "end": 175.458,
          "en": "You also get access to the request object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 175.458,
          "end": 178.978,
          "en": "under direct key, and the response object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 178.978,
          "end": 180.8,
          "en": "that will be sent back.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 180.8,
          "end": 183.713,
          "en": "And if you worked with NodeJS and Express before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 183.713,
          "end": 186.446,
          "en": "this might look familiar to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 186.446,
          "end": 189.766,
          "en": "There, you also get request and response objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 189.766,
          "end": 192.944,
          "en": "in your middleware to then work with those.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 192.944,
          "end": 195.12,
          "en": "And especially having access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 195.12,
          "end": 197.81,
          "en": "to the concrete request object can be helpful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 197.81,
          "end": 201.46,
          "en": "For example, when you're working with authentication,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 201.46,
          "end": 204.39,
          "en": "and you need to check some session cookie",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 204.39,
          "end": 205.763,
          "en": "or anything like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 205.763,
          "end": 209.91,
          "en": "This is something which I show in my full NextJS course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 209.91,
          "end": 211.54,
          "en": "it's a little too advanced here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 211.54,
          "end": 214.311,
          "en": "But you do have access to the incoming request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 214.311,
          "end": 217.55,
          "en": "and all its headers and the request body if you need to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 217.55,
          "end": 221.403,
          "en": "And that then might give you extra data or information,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 221.403,
          "end": 224.38,
          "en": "which you need for the code that executes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 224.38,
          "end": 226.315,
          "en": "in getServerSideProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 226.315,
          "end": 229.349,
          "en": "Ultimately, you then don't return a response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 229.349,
          "end": 231.772,
          "en": "by working on that response object here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 231.772,
          "end": 235.279,
          "en": "but instead, you return this object with the props key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 235.279,
          "end": 239.2,
          "en": "which holds the props for this page component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 239.2,
          "end": 241.979,
          "en": "So that is how you then can use getServerSideProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 241.979,
          "end": 246.564,
          "en": "for preparing that data for your page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 246.564,
          "end": 249.87,
          "en": "And if we do use getServerSideProps here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 249.87,
          "end": 253.118,
          "en": "if we save everything, if I reload the starting page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 253.118,
          "end": 255.336,
          "en": "you see it works just as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 255.336,
          "end": 257.79,
          "en": "and if we view the page source,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 257.79,
          "end": 260.32,
          "en": "we also see all the data in there again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 260.32,
          "end": 262.616,
          "en": "The unordered list with all the list items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 262.616,
          "end": 264.968,
          "en": "That works exactly as we learned it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 264.968,
          "end": 268.06,
          "en": "but now their page is really pre-generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 268.06,
          "end": 269.758,
          "en": "for every incoming request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 269.758,
          "end": 272.76,
          "en": "Now, which one of the two should you use?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 272.76,
          "end": 276.703,
          "en": "Is getServerSideProps better or getStaticProps?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 276.703,
          "end": 279.507,
          "en": "getServerSideProps might sound better",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 279.507,
          "end": 282.867,
          "en": "because it's guaranteed to run for every request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 282.867,
          "end": 285.886,
          "en": "But that actually can be a disadvantage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 285.886,
          "end": 289.387,
          "en": "because that means that you need to wait for your page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 289.387,
          "end": 293.82,
          "en": "to be generated on every incoming request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 293.82,
          "end": 297.57,
          "en": "Now if you don't have data that changes all the time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 297.57,
          "end": 299.09000000000003,
          "en": "and with that, I really mean",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 299.09000000000003,
          "end": 301.574,
          "en": "that it changes multiple times every second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 301.574,
          "end": 305.11,
          "en": "And if you don't need access to the request object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 305.11,
          "end": 307.176,
          "en": "let's say for authentication,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 307.176,
          "end": 310.174,
          "en": "getStaticProps is actually better.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 310.174,
          "end": 313.913,
          "en": "Because there you pre-generate an HTML file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 313.913,
          "end": 317.622,
          "en": "that file can then be stored and served by a CDN.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 317.622,
          "end": 321.113,
          "en": "And that simply is faster than regenerating",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 321.113,
          "end": 324.924,
          "en": "and fetching that data for every incoming request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 324.924,
          "end": 327.822,
          "en": "So your page will be faster when working",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 327.822,
          "end": 330.972,
          "en": "with getStaticProps, because then it can be cached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 330.972,
          "end": 334.90999999999997,
          "en": "and reused, instead of regenerated all the time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 334.90999999999997,
          "end": 338.633,
          "en": "Hence, you should really only use getServerSideProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 338.633,
          "end": 341.862,
          "en": "if you need access to that concrete request object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 341.862,
          "end": 344.813,
          "en": "because you don't have access to request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 344.813,
          "end": 346.913,
          "en": "and response in getStaticProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 347.764,
          "end": 349.873,
          "en": "Or if you really have data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 349.873,
          "end": 353.102,
          "en": "that changes multiple times every second,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 353.102,
          "end": 356.063,
          "en": "then therefore even revalidate won't help you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 356.063,
          "end": 359.84000000000003,
          "en": "then getServerSideProps is a great choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 359.84000000000003,
          "end": 361.515,
          "en": "Now here for our meetup list, though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 361.515,
          "end": 365.3,
          "en": "it's not a great choice, because that is not data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 365.3,
          "end": 366.93,
          "en": "which changes frequently.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 366.93,
          "end": 368.704,
          "en": "And here I also don't need to work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 368.704,
          "end": 370.693,
          "en": "with the incoming request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 370.693,
          "end": 374.78,
          "en": "And therefore I will comment getServerSideprops out again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 374.78,
          "end": 376.765,
          "en": "and comment getStaticProps in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 376.765,
          "end": 379.644,
          "en": "Because with that, we can take advantage of the caching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 379.644,
          "end": 383.493,
          "en": "and we're not regenerating the page multiple times,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 383.493,
          "end": 385.123,
          "en": "unnecessarily.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}